 "definition": "The documented, unbroken record of who held a piece of evidence or sample and when, used to show it was not altered.",
 "description": {
  "text": "The chronological paper trail recording who held, controlled, transferred and analyzed materials, including physical or electronic evidence. It matters most in criminal cases and is also used in civil litigation, drug testing and supply chain traceability.",
